    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "tests: generate scalars_near_split_bounds instead of hardcoding",
    "user": {
      "login": "Anshikakalpana",
      "id": 183246958,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOCuwgbg",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183246958?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anshikakalpana",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshikakalpana/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "\r\nThe hardcoded scalars_near_split_bounds array didn't match its documented formula (a*LAMBDA + (ORDER+b)/2) % ORDER. All 20 entries were off in the same 32-bit window, likely a transcription error.\r\nAs a result the vectors only reached ~126-bit outputs through secp256k1_scalar_split_lambda instead of the intended ~127-128-bit boundary, so the case they exist to test was never exercised.\r\n\r\nGenerate the values at runtime from the formula via fill_scalars_near_split_bounds(), called at each of the three sites\r\nthat use the array, instead of hardcoding them. This removes the possibility of the array drifting from its formula again.\r\n\r\nVerified the generated values reach within 1-2 units of the true k1_bound/k2_bound from the split_lambda_verify proof, confirming the existing a/b ranges are sufficient.\r\n\r\nFixes #1920.",
